        ":question/id": "17980deb-489a-5754-90d4-1d7d8ee86fdc",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\text{det}(X)$, if\n$X=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -11 \\\\ -13 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(X) & =|\\begin{aligned}-10 & -11 \\\\ -13 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-10\\cdot 7-(-11)\\cdot (-13) \\\\  & =-70-143 \\\\  & =-213\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
      "role": "independently authored inventory",
      "relationship_to_source_templates": "Previously replenished direct integer determinant ad-bc practice; authored complete operation bank and same source-shaped fixed worked solution. Independent inventory does not establish observed MA level or distractor intent."
