        ":question/problem": "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -12 \\\\ 7 & -15\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & -12 \\\\ 7 & -15\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(7)(-15)-(-12)(7) \\\\  & =-105+84 \\\\  & =-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
